WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.921
"I don't know, Waldo," Ben said. "The whole school is under quarantine.

2
00:00:08.922 --> 00:00:14.361
Plus, we're just kids. So how can we solve the mystery at Monster Academy?"

3
00:00:14.362 --> 00:00:16.949
"I don't know yet," Waldo admitted.

4
00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.960
"But what if it was my potion that caused the fog during the dance?"

5
00:00:20.961 --> 00:00:25.028
His glasses slipped down his nose, and he pushed them back up.

6
00:00:25.029 --> 00:00:31.386
"Maybe the fog from the lab traveled through the air vents to the gymnasium."

7
00:00:31.387 --> 00:00:36.650
"Could be," Ben murmured, remembering the fog inside the lab.

8
00:00:36.651 --> 00:00:40.187
"So you realize what this means, right?" said Waldo.

9
00:00:40.188 --> 00:00:43.308
"The epidemic is all my fault!"

10
00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:46.838
"It's not your fault, Waldo," Ben replied.

11
00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:53.915
"If the flu was caused by the fog from the lab, then it's someone else's fault—the monster who ruined your experiment."

12
00:00:53.916 --> 00:01:00.136
Waldo nodded, looking a little relieved. "Maybe you're right.

13
00:01:00.137 --> 00:01:05.086
But sometime soon Mr. Freaky or the nurse will trace the flu back to the lab.

14
00:01:05.087 --> 00:01:08.769
And then I'm in big trouble."

15
00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:13.999
"Well, maybe we can try to find out who tampered with your experiment," said Ben.

16
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.214
"We could find the guilty monster and make him or her confess."

17
00:01:18.215 --> 00:01:21.317
"That's what I was thinking too," said Waldo.

18
00:01:21.318 --> 00:01:25.663
"First we have to figure out what we know—all the facts.

19
00:01:25.664 --> 00:01:29.532
Then we can use those facts to figure out who our culprit is.

20
00:01:29.533 --> 00:01:32.302
We know that there was fog in the lab."

21
00:01:32.303 --> 00:01:37.797
"Another fact is that someone removed the hoses from your test tubes," Ben added.

22
00:01:37.798 --> 00:01:42.264
"And we also know that purple fog filled the gym during the dance."

23
00:01:42.265 --> 00:01:44.596
"Good," said Waldo.

24
00:01:44.597 --> 00:01:49.332
"Here are some more things we know: both my potion and the fog were purple.

25
00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:52.804
And now everybody in Monster Academy is purple."

26
00:01:52.805 --> 00:01:57.314
"And nobody was sick before the dance," added Ben.

27
00:01:57.315 --> 00:02:02.082
Suddenly Waldo's eyes lit up. "Actually, that's not true!

28
00:02:02.083 --> 00:02:07.352
Miss Bungle has been sick since before the dance—before my potion caused that fog."

29
00:02:07.353 --> 00:02:12.622
"You're right," said Ben thoughtfully. "I forgot about that.

30
00:02:12.623 --> 00:02:16.628
Hey! Maybe your potion didn't cause this epidemic at all!"

31
00:02:16.629 --> 00:02:21.989
Just then they heard voices.

32
00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:26.817
They looked over the railing and saw Mr. Freaky at the bottom of the stairs.

33
00:02:26.818 --> 00:02:30.800
The principal was with a tall human in a white coverall.

34
00:02:30.801 --> 00:02:34.732
The man was wearing a mask and carrying a clipboard.

35
00:02:34.733 --> 00:02:40.036
"That man must be the health inspector from People Place," Ben whispered.

36
00:02:40.037 --> 00:02:46.491
"So you have no idea how this epidemic started?" the health inspector said to Mr. Freaky. "No,"

37
00:02:46.492 --> 00:02:50.412
said Mr. Freaky, wringing his hands. "But

38
00:02:50.413 --> 00:02:54.032
trust me—I will find out what caused it. Mayor

39
00:02:54.033 --> 00:02:57.029
Hubbletree has nothing to worry about. Everything

40
00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:01.573
in Monster Academy is totally under control." The

41
00:03:01.574 --> 00:03:04.388
health inspector sounded doubtful. "It

42
00:03:04.389 --> 00:03:08.836
doesn't appear that things are totally under control here. Everybody

43
00:03:08.837 --> 00:03:13.771
is purple. Nobody in People Place is purple. Now,

44
00:03:13.772 --> 00:03:18.355
that's a place where things are totally under control." Mr.

45
00:03:18.356 --> 00:03:28.866
Freaky took out his handkerchief and blew his noses. "When

46
00:03:28.867 --> 00:03:33.325
did the epidemic start?" asked the health inspector. "Who

47
00:03:33.326 --> 00:03:38.737
was the first person, er, monster to get sick?" Mr.

48
00:03:38.738 --> 00:03:45.780
Freaky put away the handkerchief. "The first monster? Hmm, let's see . . . That

49
00:03:45.781 --> 00:03:49.508
would be Miss Bungle, our broom-flying instructor." Ben

50
00:03:49.509 --> 00:03:53.627
and Waldo looked at each other and smiled proudly. The

51
00:03:53.628 --> 00:03:57.139
two of them had just remembered this fact. "And

52
00:03:57.140 --> 00:04:01.400
where is she?" asked the health inspector. "She's

53
00:04:01.401 --> 00:04:04.414
at home," said Mr. Freaky. The

54
00:04:04.415 --> 00:04:08.114
health inspector made a note on his clipboard. "Show

55
00:04:08.115 --> 00:04:10.102
me the cafeteria. A

56
00:04:10.103 --> 00:04:13.546
lot of health problems occur where food is prepared. I

57
00:04:13.547 --> 00:04:16.520
want to see what you monsters are cooking." "Of

58
00:04:16.521 --> 00:04:23.984
course," said Mr. Freaky. "Follow me." Waldo

59
00:04:23.985 --> 00:04:28.602
looked at Ben and grinned. "Whew!" "I

60
00:04:28.603 --> 00:04:32.727
don't think you have anything to worry about, Waldo," said Ben. "The

61
00:04:32.728 --> 00:04:44.284
health inspector will figure out what caused the epidemic, and then someone will find a cure." Ben sighed. "

62
00:04:44.285 --> 00:04:50.795
I still have a problem though. Winnie's still mad at me."

63
00:04:50.796 --> 00:04:54.195
"I'll help you explain things to her," Waldo offered.

64
00:04:54.198 --> 00:04:59.867
"Come on, let's go find her right now."

65
00:04:59.868 --> 00:05:03.289
Ben and Waldo went downstairs to look for Winnie.

66
00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:08.162
As they passed through the lobby, a door opened, and in walked Miss Bungle!

67
00:05:08.163 --> 00:05:12.570
The ogre who worked in the main office rushed into the lobby.

68
00:05:12.571 --> 00:05:16.247
"Miss Bungle! You can't enter the building!

69
00:05:16.248 --> 00:05:19.664
Monster Academy is under quarantine!"

70
00:05:19.669 --> 00:05:22.501
The broom-flying teacher halted.

71
00:05:22.502 --> 00:05:27.210
She looked quizzically at the office ogre, and then at Ben and Waldo.

72
00:05:27.211 --> 00:05:31.550
"Why are you all . . . purple?"

73
00:05:31.551 --> 00:05:37.149
"There's an epidemic. And a quarantine!" the ogre repeated.

74
00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:39.959
"You have to leave at once!"

75
00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:45.830
Waldo stared at Miss Bungle. "Wait a second," he murmured.

76
00:05:45.831 --> 00:05:48.651
"Why are you surprised that we're all purple?

77
00:05:48.652 --> 00:05:52.946
You've been sick with the flu all week. Didn't you turn purple too?"

78
00:05:52.947 --> 00:05:55.761
Miss Bungle shook her head.

79
00:05:55.762 --> 00:06:08.347
"No, I just had a minor case of monster flu—you know, sore throat, achy joints, and small green spots."

